  "evidence": "TEXT_F: Legal annual cap on migration and monthly Rwanda flights; Mandatory National Service at 18; tougher welfare sanctions and tighter disability assessments; tougher sentences and more neighbourhood police; legislate that “sex” in the Equality Act means biological sex; NHS funding rises and tech upgrade; large tax cuts via halving employee NI and abolishing self‑employed NI. TEXT_G: A right to see a GP in 7 days and 8,000 more GPs; free personal care, a Carer’s Minimum Wage, and mental health support in every school; build 380,000 homes with 150,000 social homes, ban no‑fault evictions, expand free school meals for children in poverty; defend the Human Rights Act, strengthen disability rights, ban conversion therapy, make misogyny a hate crime; scrap Rwanda scheme, create safe and legal routes, allow work after three months, introduce flexible merit‑based visas; tax reforms including proper windfall tax and capital gains reform to fund services.",
